== principles ==
  ok   repository stores LF (index CRLF = 0; doc/measurements/ excepted as captured evidence)
  ok   no CRLF in shell scripts
  ok   build/ holds no tracked file (pure output)
  ok   no drive-letter paths in tracked shell scripts
  ok   no <stdint.h>
  ok   no 'inline' keyword
  ok   no ULL literals in the shipped library (code/)
  ok   no // comments in C sources
  ok   no post-XP Windows APIs
  ok   no temporary instrumentation tags
  ok   every 64-bit header has __int64 and long long forms under _MSC_VER
  ok   no literal %lld/%llu in code/ (use the header format macro)
  ok   app layer reads no raft config fields (budget 0, card t_972b67e8)
  ok   raft_inspect only in the diagnostics path (budget 1): allowed=['code/kserver.h:3825: if(reader.off!=reader.len||raft_inspect(server->raft,&info)!=0||treap_inspect(server->tree,&tree_info)!=0) ret']
  ok   no new bare sprintf in code/ (measured 10, budget 10, use k_text_append/k_snprintf)
  ok   no new C99 64-bit spellings in tests/ (measured 7, budget 7 = the sanctioned per-compiler blocks, use the project macros or a local layer)
  ok   raft.h/treap.h untouched in this change
  ok   every request type is accounted for in the files that must know it (21 types)
  ok   every git-derived file list is non-empty, so no rule is green for want of a file to look at (tests/ has 14 C/H files)
